# Review ownership.
#
# Left inactive deliberately. On a single-maintainer repository a CODEOWNERS
# rule enforces nothing useful - GitHub will not let you approve your own pull
# request, so a required code-owner review on a repo with one owner blocks every
# merge. The rules below are the intended ownership for when a team exists
# behind this repository; uncomment them then, and enable required reviews at
# the same time.
#
# Detection content and the pipeline that governs it:
#
#   *                    @your-org/detection-engineering
#
# Changes to what "valid" and "good" mean affect every rule in the repository,
# so they get a second reviewer:
#
#   /schemas/            @your-org/detection-engineering @your-org/soc-leads
#   /pipelines/review/   @your-org/detection-engineering @your-org/soc-leads
#   /environments/       @your-org/detection-engineering @your-org/soc-leads
